## Model card

[models.dev's exact route record](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/anomalyco/models.dev/dev/providers/opencode/models/exo-free.toml) describes a closed-weight preview with text/image input, text output, tools and high reasoning effort; **1,048,576 context / 131,072 output**, **$0 input/output**, release date **October 6, 2026**, and status **deprecated**. Its reasoning setting is explicitly not re-verified on Zen. The [current Zen catalog](https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models) does not list `exo-free`; an indexed Pi page now returns 404. Treat these as historical configuration facts, not confirmation of current callable service.

Publisher, parameter count, training architecture and knowledge cutoff remain undisclosed. The model must not be confused with Exo Labs' distributed inference software or unrelated Exo products. The recorded API is OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions. Free-tier data retention/training claims in secondary reporting lack a verified exact-route primary policy in this review.

### Raw benchmarks found

[October 7 secondary hands-on reporting](https://freeaiapi.org/articles/opencode-exo-free-guide) claims **99.4%** fingerprint similarity to Claude Opus 5.5, successful Blender scenes and useful screenshot interpretation. The article itself explains that fingerprint confidence is relative to a closed reference set. It is neither a verified publisher identity nor a capability benchmark. Its claim of a live endpoint was historical and conflicts with current deprecation/catalog evidence.

The Blender/pelican anecdotes provide no fixed task set, pass-rate protocol or reproducible numeric evaluation. No verified public exact-route GPQA/HLE, SWE/Terminal-Bench, Tau2/Tau3, GDPval-AA, vision or long-context retrieval score found in three fresh searches. Opus 5.5 scores cannot be imported from a statistical fingerprint.

